Another variant, using data.table, which should be (much?) faster than 
plyr on 2m rows. Not tested since I don't have your dataset so watch out 
for typos:

library(data.table) # assuming you installed it
df <- as.data.table(df)
dSummary <- d[,list(cru_mean_ppt = mean(cru_mean_ppt), udel_mean_ppt = 
mean(udel_mean_ppt)),by="year"]

