>
>         Dear R-langers,
>
>         This is a question about how to summarize a 4x3x2 mixed effects
>         logistic regression such that readers' eyes won't just glaze over.
>
>         What I've got is essentially the same experiment run 8 times
>         (bear with me). The experiment has three conditions. To make
>         sure that arbitrary aspects of the experimental design weren't
>         responsible for any effects, I varied one experimental parameter
>         4 ways and another one 2 ways. Hence 4x3x2.
>
>         This makes for a very long table if I want to list all the fixed
>         effects. Which I don't really want to do anyway, since they are
>         mostly uninteresting. I have around 1000 subjects, so understand
>         that it wouldn't be too bad to do model comparison. I think
>         understand how to do that for looking at the omnibus interaction:
>
>         model1 <-
>         lmer(response~(condition+__nuisance1+nuisance2)^3+(1+__condition|subject),data=__mydata,family="binomial")
>         model2 <-
